WEBVTT

00:05.094 --> 00:07.004
You're almost there.

00:07.004 --> 00:08.086
Come on, Jiron.

00:09.007 --> 00:12.007
Oink oink...

00:12.007 --> 00:17.053
Lord Ike, you can easily get up
because you use Levitation magic.

00:21.075 --> 00:24.071
Oink oink...

00:24.071 --> 00:26.013
How is it, Jiron?

00:26.013 --> 00:28.016
I think you have lost some weight.

00:29.054 --> 00:32.079
Weight is not the most important thing.
I was terrified.

00:32.079 --> 00:34.097
Have we not yet arrived
at our destination?

00:34.097 --> 00:36.072
We can already see it.

00:38.064 --> 00:39.085
Over there?

00:47.044 --> 00:48.074
This must be it.

00:48.074 --> 00:50.032
The natural nitre.

02:40.072 --> 02:47.006
THE STRONGEST MAGICIAN
IN THE DEMON LORD'S ARMY WAS A HUMAN

02:49.069 --> 02:54.003
#7 BATTLE

02:55.061 --> 02:56.099
Raise!

02:59.055 --> 03:00.058
Fire!

03:03.037 --> 03:04.004
Oink!

03:08.011 --> 03:10.038
Very good, excellent.

03:10.038 --> 03:11.075
Load the bullets!

03:13.003 --> 03:14.059
Raise!

03:15.038 --> 03:16.038
Fire!

03:34.024 --> 03:37.066
How did you fix
the city gate so quickly?

03:37.066 --> 03:39.053
What kind of magic did you use?

03:39.099 --> 03:41.079
I set up shift work.

03:42.031 --> 03:45.025
I also paid human wages.

03:46.041 --> 03:48.021
Paying human wages, huh?

03:48.021 --> 03:50.088
The general also told me about this.

03:50.088 --> 03:54.017
It works better this way than by
forcing them to work. Really amazing.

03:59.039 --> 04:00.072
This place is really small.

04:01.001 --> 04:03.085
Because this place was made
for humans in the first place.

04:04.031 --> 04:06.006
Long time no see, Ike.

04:06.006 --> 04:07.089
No, vice commander.

04:08.052 --> 04:10.003
Just call me Ike.

04:10.009 --> 04:14.053
Right now, you are vice commander,
so I need to address you as such.

04:20.016 --> 04:22.007
Everyone is here now.

04:23.058 --> 04:25.007
I think everyone has heard

04:25.007 --> 04:27.016
that Lady Cefiro has given

04:27.016 --> 04:30.055
full control of the war
to the vice commander.

04:30.055 --> 04:33.046
Everyone is now obligated
to obey Lord Ike.

04:35.059 --> 04:36.092
I have no problems with it.

04:36.092 --> 04:40.038
And I heard you really beat up Basteo.

04:40.038 --> 04:41.089
That's impressive.

04:42.025 --> 04:45.085
We three will follow
the vice commander's orders.

04:47.043 --> 04:48.043
Thank you.

04:49.085 --> 04:53.056
I have heard that the enemy
has 12,000 soldiers,

04:53.056 --> 04:55.057
but we only have 2,000 soldiers.

04:55.057 --> 04:57.049
How are we going to fight them?

04:58.004 --> 05:03.028
Crush them head-on with one against six.

05:03.028 --> 05:08.081
People in our army are not all part of
the so-called elite Werewolf Brigade.

05:09.064 --> 05:11.021
Right.

05:12.063 --> 05:14.054
How about a night raid?

05:14.054 --> 05:17.026
Nighttime is something we are used to.

05:17.092 --> 05:21.013
We know for sure
that the enemy has magicians.

05:21.097 --> 05:25.047
It is likely that they will use
Illumination or Detection to get by.

05:27.072 --> 05:29.043
What a hassle.

05:29.077 --> 05:31.064
Vice commander, what do you think?

05:31.064 --> 05:33.048
I want to fight them here.

05:33.048 --> 05:34.098
Holding the fort?

05:37.073 --> 05:41.053
The more superior a large army is, the more
vulnerable it is when it is outnumbered,

05:41.053 --> 05:44.091
and the more easily it crumbles.

05:45.087 --> 05:47.007
Let them attack here,

05:47.007 --> 05:50.026
and when their morale is at its peak,

05:50.087 --> 05:52.047
we will catch them all at once.

05:53.025 --> 05:57.073
Put an end to this war as quickly
and with as few deaths as possible.

06:25.007 --> 06:26.001
What about this?

06:26.001 --> 06:28.039
Please throw that in
the non-combustible trash.

06:35.065 --> 06:38.083
The city has become so lively.

06:40.000 --> 06:41.026
Aren't you scared?

06:42.001 --> 06:44.077
Even though some people are still scared,

06:45.031 --> 06:47.001
I am not scared.

06:47.001 --> 06:48.001
Why not?

06:48.064 --> 06:52.098
Because everyone came here
to protect this place, right?

06:53.052 --> 06:55.014
Everyone's good.

06:55.085 --> 06:58.086
It is true that there are no bad people.

06:59.032 --> 07:02.003
Yes, that makes me very happy.

07:02.003 --> 07:06.057
I am not able to fight,
but I can help make food.

07:06.057 --> 07:10.008
There are more soldiers now,
so it must be hard to make all that food.

07:10.008 --> 07:11.041
Not at all.

07:11.041 --> 07:12.083
However...

07:12.083 --> 07:13.054
What's wrong?

07:13.091 --> 07:18.088
As I consider what dishes
can be made for a large group,

07:18.088 --> 07:22.025
I realize that most of them are soups.

07:23.009 --> 07:24.009
Let me think...

07:28.068 --> 07:29.055
No!

07:29.055 --> 07:31.056
Master, don't let me bother you.

07:31.056 --> 07:34.002
What soldiers eat affects their morale.

07:34.002 --> 07:35.043
This is also part of my job.

07:36.002 --> 07:38.069
Thank goodness we don't lack food.

07:40.006 --> 07:43.073
It's all thanks to your
Norfolk four-course system.

07:45.086 --> 07:47.002
We have rice, right?

07:47.002 --> 07:50.024
Yes, we have harvested a lot.

07:51.028 --> 07:52.071
Want to try to make this food?

07:54.012 --> 07:57.016
Fried rice?

08:51.097 --> 08:54.005
So this is fried rice!

08:54.039 --> 08:56.031
This takes only a short time.

08:56.031 --> 08:58.027
We can make a lot of it.

08:58.027 --> 08:59.002
Yes!

09:04.019 --> 09:06.078
The smell of this food
makes your mouth water!

09:07.015 --> 09:09.078
It looks like it could raise
the soldiers' spirits.

09:10.061 --> 09:11.066
Let's give it a try.

09:11.066 --> 09:12.066
Okay!

09:15.007 --> 09:18.091
Why are you two eating
and leaving me out?!

09:18.091 --> 09:20.016
Do you want to have some?

09:20.058 --> 09:22.012
Yes!

09:22.063 --> 09:25.000
It looks really delicious!

09:25.000 --> 09:26.092
I heard this is known as fried rice.

09:26.092 --> 09:29.038
The name itself sounds delicious.

09:30.055 --> 09:32.005
Eh?

09:32.005 --> 09:33.076
I want to have some, too!

09:36.043 --> 09:38.047
This food is great.

09:39.031 --> 09:41.094
So delicious, it's too good!

09:42.065 --> 09:44.031
May I have another bowl?

09:49.009 --> 09:51.074
Here you go.

09:51.074 --> 09:53.041
It seems a bit too much.

09:53.041 --> 09:57.087
Eat more and get more nutrients.

09:59.005 --> 10:01.083
Do you want me to gain weight?

10:05.000 --> 10:07.092
Jeez. Can't you two just enjoy it?

10:15.034 --> 10:18.093
Lord Ike, why don't you eat?

10:18.093 --> 10:20.077
I'll eat later.

10:20.077 --> 10:22.057
How's the taste, Jiron?

10:22.057 --> 10:24.009
It's very tasty.

10:26.004 --> 10:28.086
Could this be food for our army?

10:29.025 --> 10:30.078
Of course!

10:31.086 --> 10:36.002
The rice has all the flavors
of the meat and oil in it.

10:37.002 --> 10:41.025
If this is the food, then brigades that like
meat will also be very happy, right?

10:41.025 --> 10:42.033
Is that so?

10:48.000 --> 10:49.042
The troops are assembled.

10:52.067 --> 10:54.038
The walls have been repaired.

10:57.051 --> 10:59.031
Also, the weapons are prepared.

11:01.056 --> 11:04.053
The next step is to put
our strategy into action.

11:18.007 --> 11:19.083
T-They're here!

11:23.054 --> 11:25.079
It's the Royal Alliance army!

11:26.087 --> 11:27.088
Hurry up!

11:28.005 --> 11:29.031
This way!

11:53.004 --> 11:54.057
Lord Ike!

11:56.024 --> 11:57.053
May you win big.

11:59.007 --> 12:00.078
See you later.

12:01.099 --> 12:07.000
THE STRONGEST MAGICIAN
IN THE DEMON LORD'S ARMY WAS A HUMAN

12:18.088 --> 12:20.089
If this place falls,

12:20.089 --> 12:24.085
the Royal Alliance army
will attack Arsenam!

12:25.039 --> 12:27.064
We need to make sure this doesn't happen!

12:30.006 --> 12:32.073
We must safeguard this place at all costs!

12:32.073 --> 12:33.085
Yes!

12:33.085 --> 12:35.078
Leave it to me!

12:53.009 --> 12:55.063
It's a lot smaller than I thought.

12:55.063 --> 12:57.009
It's disappointing.

12:57.009 --> 12:58.063
Yeah.

12:59.005 --> 13:02.085
We even hired the best soldiers
from other countries.

13:25.002 --> 13:27.087
This is far from being a war.

13:27.087 --> 13:29.062
This is not a war.

13:29.062 --> 13:31.046
It's a crusade.

13:31.046 --> 13:34.017
A crusade against the filthy demons.

13:35.013 --> 13:36.059
Crush them.

13:36.059 --> 13:37.086
Yes.

13:39.003 --> 13:41.051
Attack!

14:13.005 --> 14:15.021
Bright Barrier.

14:29.035 --> 14:30.006
Magic?

14:31.001 --> 14:32.089
Again.

14:32.089 --> 14:33.082
Yes.

14:58.088 --> 15:01.009
They are attacking in the usual way.

15:01.009 --> 15:03.003
Luckily, this makes my plan work.

15:03.008 --> 15:05.068
As expected of Lord Ike!

15:05.068 --> 15:08.053
You're the strongest
in the Demon Lord's army.

15:08.053 --> 15:10.076
You will not benefit
from flattering me.

15:13.031 --> 15:15.085
So, what is their next move?

15:17.035 --> 15:19.007
They like using cunning moves.

15:24.074 --> 15:26.032
Again.

15:26.032 --> 15:27.024
Yes.

15:39.013 --> 15:42.025
It is pointless, but they do it again.

15:43.005 --> 15:44.059
They are stupid.

15:45.026 --> 15:47.009
Bright Barrier.

15:57.085 --> 15:58.065
That is...

16:19.096 --> 16:20.096
Now.

16:20.096 --> 16:23.088
Yes. First squad, attack!

16:38.035 --> 16:40.048
It doesn't look like
it will end that easily.

16:44.094 --> 16:46.011
Lord Ike.

16:46.011 --> 16:48.036
The Iron Cannonball Squad is ready.

16:48.082 --> 16:50.002
It is not time yet.

16:50.002 --> 16:51.041
But...

16:52.045 --> 16:53.085
Let them take care of it first.

17:54.089 --> 17:56.026
Counterattack!

17:59.039 --> 18:01.048
Bright Barrier.

18:14.002 --> 18:17.002
We have more people than them!

18:17.002 --> 18:19.016
Charge!

18:40.006 --> 18:41.085
Don't let them get up!

18:41.085 --> 18:43.001
Hold the line!

18:54.036 --> 18:57.034
These mere demons
are quite resilient, aren't they?

18:58.003 --> 19:00.007
But it is only a matter of time.

19:00.007 --> 19:02.005
If we keep attacking like this...

19:02.005 --> 19:04.008
What's for dinner tonight?

19:04.008 --> 19:05.008
Pardon?

19:05.008 --> 19:09.025
Since dinner should be eaten quietly,
let us end it now.

19:09.025 --> 19:10.025
Yes.

19:10.075 --> 19:14.047
But how are we going to end it?

19:17.039 --> 19:19.096
Another catapult.

19:19.096 --> 19:21.077
But that would cause our men to get hurt.

19:21.077 --> 19:22.093
It doesn't matter.

19:36.007 --> 19:38.062
Bright Barrier.

19:40.074 --> 19:41.007
Get down!

19:44.062 --> 19:45.083
Oink?!

20:14.009 --> 20:15.086
Oink!

20:24.066 --> 20:26.033
Those guys...

20:26.033 --> 20:28.029
They even kill their comrades.

21:06.062 --> 21:09.004
Second squad, attack!

21:19.097 --> 21:21.034
This is bad!

21:21.034 --> 21:22.093
Don't let them into the city!

23:34.052 --> 23:38.044
THE DECISIVE BATTLE OF IVALIES
